-- Q1016: Trusts and Estates [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 665, the throwback rules for accumulation distributions were largely repealed for domestic trusts by the Tax Reform Act of 1997. Accumulation distributions from domestic trusts are taxed to beneficiaries as ordinary income in the year of distribution under Section 662, without throwback treatment or look-back computation.
Wrong (A): The throwback rules that would tax the distribution as if made in Year 1 were repealed for domestic trusts. Only foreign trusts remain subject to throwback under Section 665.
Wrong (B): There is no double taxation. The trust pays tax in Year 1 on retained income, and the Year 2 distribution is taxed to the beneficiary with the trust receiving a distribution deduction under Section 661.
Wrong (D): The distribution is not tax-exempt. The beneficiary must include it in gross income in the year received under Section 662.$EXPL$
