-- Q1018: Trusts and Estates [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 441(b)(2) and Section 644, a decedent''s estate may elect any fiscal year ending within 12 months of the date of death on its first Form 1041. This flexibility allows the executor to control the timing of income distributions and the Section 661 distribution deduction. For Robert, the estate could elect any month-end from October 2025 through August 2026.
Wrong (A): Estates are not required to use the calendar year. Unlike trusts under Section 644(a), estates have unrestricted fiscal year flexibility.
Wrong (C): The fiscal year need not end on the date of death anniversary. The executor may choose any month-end within the 12-month period following death.
Wrong (D): The estate''s tax year is independent of the decedent''s individual tax year. There is no requirement to match the decedent''s prior filing period.$EXPL$
