  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 336(a), a liquidating corporation generally recognizes both gains and losses on distributed property as if sold at FMV. The corporation recognizes a $50,000 loss ($150,000 FMV minus $200,000 basis). Loss disallowance under Section 336(d) may apply for related-party distributions, but the general rule permits loss recognition.
