-- Q1035: Entity Formation and Liquidation [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 357(c), when liabilities assumed by the corporation exceed the transferor''s basis in the contributed property, the excess is recognized as gain. Here, the liability assumed ($120,000) exceeds basis ($100,000) by $20,000, which the shareholder must recognize. The shareholder''s stock basis becomes $0.
Wrong (A): Zero gain would apply only if the liability did not exceed basis. Since $120,000 exceeds $100,000, Section 357(c) requires recognition of the $20,000 excess.
Wrong (C): The $60,000 figure ($160,000 FMV minus $100,000 basis) represents the total realized gain, but Section 357(c) limits recognition to the excess of liabilities over basis, not the full appreciation.
Wrong (D): Recognizing the full $120,000 liability as gain ignores that basis offsets the liability. Only the excess of liabilities over basis ($20,000) triggers gain under Section 357(c).$EXPL$
