  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 199A, eligible taxpayers may deduct up to 20% of qualified business income from pass-through entities. With 80% of income taxed at the owner''s 37% marginal rate, the effective rate is 80% x 37% = 29.6%. This single level of taxation compares favorably to the C corporation''s 21% entity-level rate, which faces additional shareholder tax upon distribution.
