  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 1402(a), a general partner''s entire distributive share of partnership ordinary business income is subject to self-employment tax (15.3% up to the Social Security wage base, 2.9% Medicare above that), regardless of whether the income is actually distributed. This is a key disadvantage compared to S corporations.
